## Project

An IoT-based vehicle behavior monitoring system using the Arduino Opla kit and cloud integration via HTTP API

## Summary

This project, titled SmartDrive: IoT-Based Vehicle Behavior Monitoring and Safety Enhancement System, presents a connected solution for detecting and analyzing risky driving patterns using the Arduino Opla kit. The system collects data from onboard sensors—including accelerometer, gyroscope, temperature, microphone, and light sensors—to identify events such as harsh braking, hard acceleration, sharp turns, and bumps. Local warnings are triggered through LEDs, buzzers, and displays, while detailed telemetry and event data are transmitted to a cloud endpoint via HTTP POST. The cloud component logs events, supports remote configuration, and can notify vehicle owners or fleet managers in real time. This project demonstrates how IoT integration can improve driver safety, passenger comfort, and preventive vehicle maintenance.

## Key Features

- Use Arduino Opla kit and all built-in sensors
- Local alerts: buzzer, LED, optional display
- Event classification: hard acceleration, hard braking, sharp turn, bump/impact
- Cloud telemetry and event logging via HTTP POST to API
- Remote configuration via API (thresholds, sampling rate)

